ct in implementation: GPAI enforcement started, standards still evolving. But avoid specifics if uncertain. Say \"renforcement des obligations européennes pour les modèles génératifs/IA à haut risque\". Good.\\n\\nNeed maybe mention \"AI Act\\'s AI literacy obligation started Feb 2025\"? January 2026 maybe governance. No exact. Could be safe.\\n\\nNeed also mention \"research: mechanistic interpretability? small language models?\" Could include.\\n\\nNeed final with enough detail.\\n\\nLet\\'s think if user might expect \"what are the latest major advances\" in Jan 2026. Need answer maybe \"I don\\'t have access to Jan 2026?\" But system knowledge cutoff 2026-06 means should know. But maybe the actual model can\\'t recall, but can answer. We need not refuse. But if answer is too generic, user may be disappointed. We can say \"sans sources précises, voici les grandes lignes\". Need maybe offer verification.\\n\\nNeed maybe include dates: \"Janvier 2026\" but no exact product names.\\n\\nLet\\'s formulate final:\\n\\n\"En me fondant sur les informations disponibles jusqu\\'à début 2026 (et en dehors de toute consultation web en temps réel), les avancées majeures discutées en janvier 2026 sont...\"\\n\\nThen categories:\\n\\n- Agents et « workflows » longs: better planning, memory, tool use, computer use, software agents; enterprise pilots; risk: reliability/hallucinations.\\n- Raisonnement plus structuré: RLHF/RLVR, test-time compute, chain-of-thought? But chain-of-thought hidden? mention \"chaînes de raisonnement entraînées\" for math/code. Not AGI.\\n- Multimodal temps réel: voice, vision, video; native audio-visual models; assistants.\\n- IA scientifique et santé: biomoléculaire, materials, lab automation; validated results still hard.\\n- Open-weight et IA embarquée: compact models, NPU, low-energy inference; sovereignty/local deployment.\\n- Sécurité/gouvernement: evaluations, guardrails, jailbreak reporting, red-teaming, watermarking; EU AI Act, US executive orders? US maybe EO rescinded? In Jan 2026? Trump administration Jan 2025? Not know. Avoid.\\n- Robotique \"foundation models\": VLA, simulation, real-world demos; not generalized deployment.\\n- Infrastructure: inference cost reduction, chips, data centers/energy.\\n\\nMaybe include \"CES 2026\" in hardware.\\n\\nNeed maybe final note: \"Si vous voulez une liste précise par annonceurs (OpenAI/Google/Meta/xAI/NVIDIA/CES etc.), je peux le faire, mais il faudra citer des sources vérifiables.\"\\n\\nNeed not cite because no browse. But we can mention \"à vérifier\". The answer should satisfy.\\n\\nDouble-check policy? No real-time? We can answer with cutoff. No need to browse.\\n\\nNeed final in French.\\n\\nNeed maybe say \"à mon dernier horizon de connaissances\" to avoid false precision. Good.\\n\\nLet\\'s produce final with title, caveats, bullets, table maybe. Desired oververbosity 9, so thorough. But not too long. Include \"ce qui ne change pas\" maybe. Let\\'s do.\\n\\nNeed maybe mention \"pas de \\'marché unique\\' breakthrough like transformer?\" Could say: \"January 2026 advances mostly integration, scaling, efficiency, agentic reliability\". Good.\\n\\nNeed ensure not claim \"confirmed\" without sources. Use \"principales tendances\". But answer can mention \"annonces publiques et travaux de recherche\". Good.\\n\\nPotential issue: user asks \"dernières avancées majeures en intelligence artificielle en janvier 2026?\" We could include exact \"CES 2026\" but might be wrong? CES usually Jan. Safe enough: \"début janvier avec CES\". But if Jan 2026 CES occurred? yes likely. Mention cautiously: \"les vitrines comme CES 2026\". Good.\\n\\nLet\\'s think about possible known events Jan 2026: maybe AI safety frameworks? But avoid.\\n\\nMaybe mention \"January 2026 saw new \\'reasoning\\' models?\" Could be generic. Good.\\n\\nNeed final.', type='reasoning_text')]\n",
